    "heading": "に — Where something IS, where you GO",
    "text": "に is the particle for <strong>destination, location, point in time and recipient</strong>. It answers the questions \"Where to?\", \"Where?\" (for existence), \"When?\" (for specific points in time) and \"To whom?\". Of all the particles, に is probably the most versatile — it shows up in a wide range of contexts, but it always has to do with some kind of \"target point\".",
    "tip": "Time expressions with に: specific points in time (clock times, days of the week, dates) need に. Relative time expressions like 今日, 明日, 来週 do NOT take に, because they already express a time relationship to \"now\".",
